        {
          "id": 594422871,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Reload is hidden on purpose. I am not sure if this is the best approach. Reloading a model should only be done in certain scenarios, and I am not sure, if I have not misnamed the function here in the first place. In my opinion the functionality should rather be implemented by conforming to the Qt Model concept and implementing \"revert()\" for the model, which will only clear the storage internally and call \"invalidate()\" on the model. Is a cleaner and much more standardized approach.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
